{"id": "x0084", "pool": "easy-fact", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "In a car, an SU, Weber, or Ze nith typically refers to types of carbure tors. These are mechanical devices that mix fuel and air for internal combustion engine s. The SU is often associated with the Solex company, which made popular carburetors in Europe. We ber was a German manufacturer known for high-performance car buretors used in racing cars. Zen ith was another brand that produced various styles of carbure tors, sometimes used in European vehicles. So, in short, they're different brands or models of car buretors found in older cars before electronic fuel injection became common.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 31, "carrier_ended": null}
