{"id": "x0188", "pool": "easy-chat", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Cockney rhyming s lang is a type of slang that originated in the East End of London and uses rhym ing words to replace or substitute common words. Here are some examples of cock ney rhyming slang: apple and p ear for \" ear,\" meaning you might say, \"I can't hear you\" as \" I can' t apple and pear you.\"B read and butter for \" money,\" so someone might ask, \"How much bread and butter have you got?\" to mean how much money do you have?Ch airlift for \"lift,\" which means elevator or ho listic lift. So if someone says they're going up the chairlift, they mean they're going up the elevator.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 41, "carrier_ended": null}
