{"id": "x0260", "pool": "easy-chat", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The expense ratio for an ETF is the annual fee charged by the fund manager to cover operational costs. It's usually expressed as a percentage of the fund' s assets and can range from less than 0.1% for some broad market index funds to around 0.5% or higher for more specialized ET Fs like sector or international ones. Generally, lower expense ratios are better because they mean more of your investment returns stay in your pocket over time.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 25, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0268", "pool": "easy-chat", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Okay, so I have a few tips for you. First of all, make sure your bike is clean and free from any dirt or debris that can create drag. Next, consider using an aerodynamic frame design, such as a time trial or tri ath lon bike, which is specifically designed to reduce air resistance. You can also add aerodynamic wheel s, like deep section wheels or disc wheels, which can significantly reduce drag. Additionally, use a low-profile saddle and handlebar setup to minimize the wind resistance created by your body position. Finally, wear form-f itting clothing, like tight sp andex jerseys and short s, to further reduce drag caused by loose fabric s flapping in the wind.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 43, "carrier_ended": null}
