{"id": "x0692", "pool": "know-open", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "After the Babylonian captivity, the Jews returned to Jerusalem and began rebuilding the temple under the leadership of Zerubbabel.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0700", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 23, "onset_chunk": 22, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The teacher is telling the student to change only the type of hand soap because it improves the reliability of the results. By keeping all other variables, like the type of bacter ium tested, constant, the experiment can isolate the effect of changing just one variable— in this case, the hand soap. This helps ensure that any differences observed in bacterial kill are due to the different types of soap rather than other factors. So, the correct answer is B: improves the reliability of the results.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 26, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0708", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 18, "onset_chunk": 17, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is C. Wood grows more quickly than coal forms. Wood is considered a renewable resource because trees can be replanted and grow back relatively fast, while coal takes millions of years to form from organic matter under high pressure and temperature, making it non-re newable on human timescale s.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0716", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 16, "onset_chunk": 15, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The best answer would be A, a can teloupe. This is because the moon is about one quarter the size of Earth. So using an orange to represent the moon means you'd need something larger than that to show Earth accurately. Among the options given, a can teloupe is the largest fruit listed, making it the most suitable choice for representing Earth in this scale model.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0724", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 19, "onset_chunk": 18, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, that's a good question. The reason the tile feels colder is because it conduct s heat better than the carpet. So when you stand on it, your body heat transfers more quickly to the tile, making it feel cold er even if both are at the same temperature. Carpet, on the other hand, doesn' t conduct heat as well, so it feels warmer. That means the answer is B: the tile floor conduct s heat better than the carpet.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0732", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 17, "onset_chunk": 16, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A nail is left outside and it rusts. This one results in a different kind of material being formed because the iron in the nail reacts with oxygen and water to form rust, which is a completely new substance. The other options involve breaking or shaping existing materials without changing their chemical composition.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 17, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0740", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is D, season changes. The tilt of Earth's axis causes the different seasons as it orbits the Sun.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0748", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 17, "onset_chunk": 17, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Let's think about this. A lunar eclipse happens when the Earth comes between the Sun and the Moon, so the Earth blocks sunlight from reaching the Moon. That means it's not option B or C. Option D is about a 90-degree angle, which doesn't fit either. So the correct answer has to be A, when Earth is between the Moon and the Sun.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0756", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 29, "onset_chunk": 16, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The best method to determine which type of popcor n produces the most popped kernel s is B, design an experiment that tests multiple types of popcorn using repeated trials. This approach allows you to control variables and collect reliable data by comparing different kinds under consistent conditions.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0764", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is B. High turbidity means the water is cloudy or murky due to suspended particles like soil and organic matter. This usually indicates that the water may be contaminated with bacteria, pathogen s, or other harmful substances, making it un safe to drink without treatment. While turbid ity can sometimes correlate with other factors like chemical contamination, it doesn' t directly indicate pH levels or temperature. Therefore, the most likely conclusion is that it is unsafe to drink.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 29, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0772", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The factor that would most likely limit the number of mice living in an area is more predator s. While plenty of resources and a stable climate help support population growth, predators directly reduce mouse numbers by hunting them. Even if food and shelter are abundant, increased predation pressure can keep the population low. So, more predator s would be the primary limiting factor.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 20, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0780", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 19, "onset_chunk": 18, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Newton's second law of motion states that acceleration is directly proportional to the net force acting on an object, assuming mass remains constant. So if the force is increased four times, the acceleration will also increase four times. The correct answer is B, four times.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0788", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 16, "onset_chunk": 16, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "If two forces act in opposite directions on a wood block and they are unbalanced, the position of the block will change. The correct answer is D. When forces are un balanced, there is a net force acting on the object, which causes it to accelerate or move in the direction of the larger force. So, the block will move, changing its position. It will not balance the forces itself, reverse direction unless acted upon by another force, or change mass due to these forces alone.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 27, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0796", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The weight of an object changes at different locations on Earth because the gravitational force varies slightly due to differences in distance from the Earth's center and variations in the planet's mass distribution. Among the options given, 16 newtons is a measurement of weight, as it represents the force exerted by gravity on an object.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
